# SCSS Style Rules

- Do only minimal required changes, do not rewrite properties without asking.
- For any solutions follow the same pattern as already used in the project.

## Nesting

- Reflect the DOM hierarchy in SCSS nesting: child elements are nested inside their parent selector.
- BEM modifiers (`&.modifier`) are nested inside the block they modify.
- Pseudo-elements and pseudo-classes (`&::placeholder`, `&:hover`) are nested inside their element.

## Order inside a selector

1. Own properties (layout, sizing, colors, etc.)
2. State modifiers (`&.modifier`)
3. Child elements (`.child {}`)
4. Pseudo-elements (`&::before`, `&::after`)

## Example

```scss
.block {
  // own properties

  &.blockModifier {
    // modifier overrides
  }

  .child {
    // child properties

    &.childModifier {
      // child modifier
    }
  }

  &::placeholder {
    // pseudo-element
  }
}
```

## Do not

- Do not write child or modifier selectors as flat top-level classes if they logically belong inside a parent.
- Do not repeat the parent selector manually — use `&`.
